    "title": "Fill Eclipse fixed-size map slots through direct key/value traversal"
  },
  "review_statement": "## Problem and change\n\nThe small immutable-map finisher materialized temporary Pairs through keyValuesView before filling its existing key/value array. Use forEachKeyValue to fill those slots directly. Preserve empty through three-entry factory behavior, null/collision handling, traversal order, and oversized-map behavior.\n\nUpdate the real generator template and release note; add four differential/JSON regression methods, including 512 null/collision combinations.\n\n## Verification\n\nActual complete reactor on the final notice-complete template: **494 tests, zero failures/errors/skips**: Guava 327, HPPC 23, Eclipse 97, and PCollections 47. The R2 run used the existing cached snapshot dependencies offline. The dated modification notice retains the original Apache licence header.\n\nThe template is generator data. Canonical text admission is bound to the exact crate, path, before digest, and after digest; ordinary Java still requires the typed parser. The current M3JDK tree has no corresponding receiving adapter owner, so no new adapter runtime dependency was imported.\n\n## Canonical execution\n\nCanonical recipe: `com.synexia.m3jdk.CollectionsContractRefinement20261017`, source revision **7af83c5ee4ad166d8cd45c6c33822debabd705ca**, review https://github.com/hsoliwal/com.synexia/pull/15427. Product bytes were emitted by actual qualified SDK Results and the second receive changed zero files. The canonical recipe and executable receiver remain in Synexia.\n",
